{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" product to the test target. "},{"code":"withRecordingTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" binds a fresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker to the test’s task for the length of its body, then returns every event tracked in it, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Here "},{"code":"SignedUp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Testing","import TrackerTesting","","@Test func signingUpTracksThePlan() async {","    let tracked = await withRecordingTracker {","        Tracker.current.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","    }","    #expect(tracked.events(of: SignedUp.self) == [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")])","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call has a tracker of its own, so tests running at the same time never see each other’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events. The body may be sync or async, and may return a value, read as "},{"code":"tracked.value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"tracked.names","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every event’s name and "},{"code":"tracked.records","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" every record."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most code needs nothing more: it tracks through ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which falls back to the tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the app bootstrapped, and the test’s binding wins over that one. A view whose tracker was never set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that binds its tracker with ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reaches the test’s tracker too. Pass a tracker instead where the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"code reads one set for a single view tree. A tracker given to a SwiftUI view with ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", such as a preview’s,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reaches the view’s environment but not code that reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Such a test takes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker the body is given and sets it on the view: ","type":"text"},{"code":"withRecordingTracker { tracker in … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","identifi